{
  "assessment_scope": "Final assessment of the complete local v2-retirement implementation, current governance and package consumers, required independent reviews and exact Git/PR handoff basis.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-11-retire-v2-record-format",
  "changes": [
    "RigorLoop operates on v3 stores and removes the v2 validator, dispatch, recovery, schemas, templates and exclusive test resources.",
    "Discovery and provenance consumers recognize historical archives through bounded format headers while preserving current-store errors and transaction attention.",
    "Canonical skills, governance, package inputs and example guidance use the supported contract; shared safety tests retain their protection on v3."
  ],
  "evidence_refs": [
    {
      "id": "tg00-pre-removal-disposition",
      "path": "docs/changes/2026-09-11-retire-v2-record-format/evidence.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "m1-implementation",
      "path": "docs/changes/2026-09-11-retire-v2-record-format/evidence.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "m2-implementation",
      "path": "docs/changes/2026-09-11-retire-v2-record-format/evidence.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "final-verification",
      "path": "docs/changes/2026-09-11-retire-v2-record-format/evidence.json"
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No new v2-retirement, rejection or archival-compatibility tests were added, as requested; retirement-specific branches were assessed statically.",
    "Historical dependency closure covers the inspected local repository; no completion or migration is claimed for external v2 stores.",
    "Local validation does not establish hosted CI, PR creation, merge, release publication or customer activation."
  ],
  "outcome": "success",
  "rationale": [
    "The responsible pre-removal disposition accounts for the selected historical work and recovery obligations without converting old judgments.",
    "The retained execution evidence and independently reviewed implementation agree on v3 behavior, safe storage mechanics and separately versioned request/response contracts.",
    "Fresh whole-change Code Review assesses both milestones and their interactions; the final engineering subjects match the exact tested candidate.",
    "Current workflow, concerns and applicability support closeout, and later evidence-only commits do not change the verified engineering basis."
  ],
